      "artist": "Mike Calder, image of  Civitas Londinium, Agas' Map of London, c. 1570-1605",
      "description": "The earliest proper map (as opposed to panorama) of London known.  Attributed to Ralph Agas, and probably surveyed between 1570 and 1605. The original was 6 foot 0.5 inches long by 2 feet 4.5 inches wide.  This much reduced image is a scan of a copy of a lithograph of a copy, was itself badly repaired with sellotape and has had to be \"restored\"; so is hardly a truly faithful representation of the original, but few good copies exist and no other detailed public domain images are known.",
